# Pokemon TCG UI - Walkthrough

## Overview
I have successfully built a beautiful, responsive user interface using CodeIgniter 3 to display Pokemon TCG sets and cards using your local JSON data, now featuring live market prices!

### Features Implemented
1. **Model Layer ([Pokemon_model.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/pokemon/application/models/Pokemon_model.php))**: Added methods to parse [sets/en.json](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/pokemon/pokemon-tcg-data-master/pokemon-tcg-data-master/sets/en.json) and `cards/en/{set_id}.json`.
2. **Controller Layer ([Pokemon.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/pokemon/application/controllers/Pokemon.php))**: Added endpoints `/pokemon` (for Sets), `/pokemon/cards/{id}` (for Cards List), and `/pokemon/card/{setId}/{cardId}` (for Card Details).
3. **Routing**: Updated [config/routes.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/pokemon/application/config/routes.php) to set the default controller to `pokemon` and specifically configured the URL for `localhost:81`.
4. **View Layer & UI**: 
   - Created a modern, glassmorphic UI using custom CSS and the "Outfit" Google Font.
   - Added grid layouts for both Sets and Cards views.
5. **Card Details Page**: Clicking on any card opens a dedicated details page. This page shows the large, high-res version of the card, along with formatted views of the card's HP, types, rarity, abilities, attacks, and flavor text.
6. **Live Market Prices**: Integrated the `api.pokemontcg.io` API. When viewing the cards list or the card details page, JavaScript asynchronously fetches real-time TCGPlayer market data and beautifully overlays color-coded price badges on the cards!

### How to Verify
1. Open your browser.
2. Navigate to: `http://localhost:81/pokemon/index.php/pokemon/`
3. Click on any set (e.g., Base Set) to see its cards load. Notice the beautiful new green/purple gradient price tags on the top right corners of the cards!
4. **Click directly on a card's image or panel**. This will instantly take you to the new custom Card Details page to see all of its attacks and super-sized art.
